Companion to PR #28114: same bug in Bedrock converse_transformation.

When response_format falls back to the synthetic json_tool_call tool
(because supports_native_structured_output is False), Bedrock's
converse transformation also force-sets tool_choice if not
is_thinking_enabled. Same bug as in anthropic/chat/transformation.py:
is_thinking_enabled doesn't recognise adaptive, so adaptive-thinking
models still get forced tool_choice and Bedrock returns
"Thinking may not be enabled when tool_choice forces tool use".

Mirror the fix here. Drop once upstream PR catches up.

--- a/litellm/llms/bedrock/chat/converse_transformation.py
+++ b/litellm/llms/bedrock/chat/converse_transformation.py
@@ -1014,11 +1014,17 @@
                 optional_params=optional_params, tools=[_tool]
             )

+            # Adaptive thinking models (Claude 4.7+) need the same carve-out
+            # as anthropic/chat/transformation.py: is_thinking_enabled does
+            # not match thinking.type=="adaptive", so without this check we
+            # set a forced tool_choice while thinking is on the wire body
+            # and Bedrock rejects with "Thinking may not be enabled when
+            # tool_choice forces tool use".
             if (
                 litellm.utils.supports_tool_choice(
                     model=model, custom_llm_provider=self.custom_llm_provider
                 )
-                and not is_thinking_enabled
+                and not (is_thinking_enabled or AnthropicConfig._is_adaptive_thinking_model(model))
             ):
                 optional_params["tool_choice"] = ToolChoiceValuesBlock(
                     tool=SpecificToolChoiceBlock(name=RESPONSE_FORMAT_TOOL_NAME)
